{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>When He made the skies firm above</b> — it is an expression of strength and firmness. Its meaning is like the meaning of <b>בהכינו</b> (when He established)." "<b>בעזוז</b> — it is an expression of עוז, meaning strength and firmness. It is an infinitive, a שלם [complete] form, and strength and firmness were borrowed for waters, as in: 'and in mighty waters a path.' So too intensity was borrowed for it in the statement 'the mighty waters of the river.'"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:33.024723901Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}